    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n57361" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῐθᾰρῳδ-ός</span></b> , ὁ,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κιθάρα, ἀοιδός</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who plays and sings to the cithara</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.547
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pherecr.
				6.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Mus.</u>
				p.28K.
			</span></i>, etc.: as fem., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. γυνή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alciphr.
					3.33
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>a fish</i>, found in the Red Sea, with body striped
			like the strings of a lyre, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				11.23
			</span></i>.</div>
